<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<worksheet xml:id="biostats-act-13" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
    <title>🏫 Activity 13 - Tests of Independence </title>

    <introduction>
        <p> This assignment is due at the beginning of class on <alert> Wednesday, November 4</alert>. It is graded based on completeness according to the rubric available on Canvas. You are encouraged to use your notes and collaborate with your group members to complete this activity. </p>

        
    </introduction>

    <exercise>
        <introduction>
            <p>
                The tables below contain the results from 30 experiments on various bacteria types, including Bacillus, Escherichia Coli, Pseudomonas, and Staphylococcus. Cultures of each bacteria were grown across four media: Agar, Blood, Broth, and Gelatin. Each culture was administered an antibiotic its response was categorized as either Immune (I), Resistant (R), Neutral (N), or Susceptible (S).  
            </p>
            <table>
                <title>Bacillus Data</title>
                <tabular>
                    <row header="yes">
                        <cell>Culture</cell>
                            <cell>1</cell>
                            <cell>2</cell>
                            <cell>3</cell>
                            <cell>4</cell>
                            <cell>5</cell>
                            <cell>6</cell>
                            <cell>7</cell>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <cell>Medium</cell>
                            <cell>Agar</cell>
                            <cell>Agar</cell>
                            <cell>Blood</cell>
                            <cell>Blood</cell>
                            <cell>Broth</cell>
                            <cell>Broth</cell>
                            <cell>Geletin</cell>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <cell>Response</cell>
                            <cell>N</cell>
                            <cell>N</cell>
                            <cell>N</cell>
                            <cell>N</cell>
                            <cell>N</cell>
                            <cell>I</cell>
                            <cell>S</cell>
                    </row>
                </tabular>
            </table>

